# Pinned host keys for gitlab.com, published at
# https://docs.gitlab.com/user/gitlab_com/#ssh-host-keys-fingerprints
#
# Used as UserKnownHostsFile for every clone/pull/push in gitlab_git.py so host
# verification never falls back to StrictHostKeyChecking=no or to trust-on-first-use.
# A project pointing at a self-hosted GitLab may instead supply its own file via the
# GITLAB_SSH_KNOWN_HOSTS environment variable -- but that variable is only ever visible
# to an interactive shell that set it, never to a real `usine.py spawn` (isolated env)
# and never portable to a different machine. This deployment's one self-hosted
# instance (gitlab.dom.tti, Talan_Factory's `git.url`) is pinned directly below instead,
# same as gitlab.com -- these are host PUBLIC keys, not secrets; pinning one doesn't
# grant any access, it only lets git recognize a server it already expects to talk to.
#
# Re-verify these against the URL above (or your own `ssh-keyscan <host>` compared
# out-of-band against the host's published fingerprints) before trusting them blindly.
